1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,000
Can I help you?

2
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:05,379
Yes, I've just moved to this area with my wife and children

3
00:00:05,379 --> 00:00:09,055
and I'd like to know where we can all register with a doctor at

4
00:00:09,055 --> 00:00:10,100
a Health Centre.

5
00:00:10,100 --> 00:00:12,054
Okay.

6
00:00:12,054 --> 00:00:15,620
Well, there's Doctor Green at The Harvey Clinic.

7
00:00:15,620 --> 00:00:17,260
We always recommend her for babies,

8
00:00:17,260 --> 00:00:20,540
because she's very good with them and she runs a special clinic.

9
00:00:20,540 --> 00:00:23,181
Oh…actually my youngest child is five,

10
00:00:23,181 --> 00:00:26,200
so that wouldn't be any good for us.

11
00:00:26,200 --> 00:00:27,380
Right.

12
00:00:27,380 --> 00:00:30,190
Is there anywhere else I could try?

13
00:00:30,190 --> 00:00:35,610
Yes, the Eshcol Health Practice is the next one on my list.

14
00:00:35,610 --> 00:00:36,790
How do you spell that?

15
00:00:36,790 --> 00:00:36,840
E-S-H-C-O-L.

16
00:00:36,840 --> 00:00:40,067
And it's Doctor Fuller,

17
00:00:40,067 --> 00:00:44,000
who has space on his list.

18
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:46,120
The clinic only opened a year ago,

19
00:00:46,120 --> 00:00:48,240
so the facilities are all very modern.

20
00:00:48,240 --> 00:00:49,280
That sounds good.

21
00:00:49,280 --> 00:00:52,924
And it's particularly good if you're busy during the day,

22
00:00:52,924 --> 00:00:55,840
because they also do appointments in the evening.

23
00:00:55,840 --> 00:00:57,950
They're closed on Saturday, though.

24
00:00:57,950 --> 00:01:02,320
The only other place on the list is the Health Centre on Shore Lane.

25
00:01:02,320 --> 00:01:07,840
You can register with Doctor Gormley,

26
00:01:07,840 --> 00:01:09,680
that's G-O-R-M-L-E-Y.

27
00:01:09,680 --> 00:01:13,220
He's new there,but the centre has a very good reputation.

28
00:01:13,220 --> 00:01:16,239
Oh yes, I thnik I know the road.

29
00:01:16,239 --> 00:01:18,503
That would be the best one.

30
00:01:18,503 --> 00:01:18,880
Thanks.

31
00:01:18,880 --> 00:01:22,390
Could you tell me, will all their services be free?

32
00:01:22,390 --> 00:01:27,240
Erm… there are usually some small charges that doctors make.

33
00:01:27,240 --> 00:01:30,880
Let me see what it says about the Shore Lane Centre.

34
00:01:30,880 --> 00:01:33,915
If you need to be vaccinated before any trips abroad.

35
00:01:33,915 --> 00:01:36,040
you won't have to pay for this.

36
00:01:36,040 --> 00:01:37,621
Erm, what else?

37
00:01:37,621 --> 00:01:44,996
The sports injury treatment service operates on a paying basis, as does the nutritional

38
00:01:44,996 --> 00:01:46,050
therapy service.

39
00:01:46,050 --> 00:01:51,930
Some health centres do offer alternative therapies like homeopathy as part of their pay-to-use

40
00:01:51,930 --> 00:01:52,350
service.

41
00:01:52,350 --> 00:01:57,780
Shore Lane are hoping to do this soon-I think they may start with acupuncture.

42
00:01:57,780 --> 00:02:02,564
And finally, if you need to prove you're healthy or haven't had any serious

43
00:02:02,564 --> 00:02:07,348
injuries before a new employer will accept you, you can get a free fitness

44
00:02:07,348 --> 00:02:08,031
check-up there,

45
00:02:08,031 --> 00:02:11,790
but you'd most likely have to pay for insurance medicals though.

46
00:02:11,790 --> 00:02:13,400
Okay, thanks.

47
00:02:13,400 --> 00:02:18,199
You might also be interested to know the Centre is running a pilot scheme

48
00:02:18,199 --> 00:02:19,570
of talks for patients.

49
00:02:19,570 --> 00:02:21,445
I've got the list here.

50
00:02:21,445 --> 00:02:23,320
Actually, they look very interesting.

51
00:02:23,320 --> 00:02:24,870
What sort of things?

52
00:02:24,870 --> 00:02:27,650
Well, the first one's about giving up smoking.

53
00:02:27,650 --> 00:02:32,117
It's next week, the twenty-fifth of February, at 7 pm,

54
00:02:32,117 --> 00:02:34,350
and that's in Room 4.

55
00:02:34,350 --> 00:02:39,942
It says, the talk will stress the health benefits particularly for people with asthma

56
00:02:39,942 --> 00:02:41,140
or heart disease.

57
00:02:41,140 --> 00:02:42,500
That sounds very interesting.

58
00:02:42,500 --> 00:02:45,557
There's also a talk for families with children.

59
00:02:45,557 --> 00:02:47,086
It's on Healthy Eating,

60
00:02:47,086 --> 00:02:51,290
and takes place on the first of March at five o'clock.

61
00:02:51,290 --> 00:02:52,790
Will that be at the Health Centre?

62
00:02:52,790 --> 00:02:56,607
Erm, actually it's at the primary school on Shore Lane.

63
00:02:56,607 --> 00:03:01,570
I imagine they're inviting the parents of pupils there-it says here 'all welcome.'

64
00:03:01,570 --> 00:03:04,260
Mmm, I might go to that if I have time.

65
00:03:04,260 --> 00:03:10,210
There's a couple of other talks-one giving advice about how to avoid injuries while

66
00:03:10,210 --> 00:03:11,060
doing exercise.

67
00:03:11,060 --> 00:03:13,509
It's on the ninth of March.

68
00:03:13,509 --> 00:03:17,181
Oh, it's a late afternoon talk, at four thirty,

69
00:03:17,181 --> 00:03:19,630
and it'll be in Room 6.

70
00:03:19,630 --> 00:03:24,290
It also says the talk is suitable for all ages.

71
00:03:24,290 --> 00:03:28,950
And finally, there's a talk called 'Stress Management' which is…
